1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,170
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

2
00:00:05,338 --> 00:00:08,925
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

3
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:14,264
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

4
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:19,769
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

5
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:23,106
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you ♪</i>

6
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:25,233
<i>♪ Everything changed? ♪</i>

7
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:28,111
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

8
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:32,240
<i>♪ Because I'm coming home ♪</i>

9
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:37,287
[BILLY] <i>You know, I'm sure</i>
<i>that they are both proud of you.</i>

10
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:38,788
<i>Look.</i>

11
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:41,458
<i>You got everything you wanted.</i>

12
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,420
[JORDAN] <i>Not quite yet.</i>

13
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:52,552
<i>What's this drama?</i>

14
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>You're so serious!</i>

15
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,222
<i>Dude.</i>

16
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:59,225
<i>- My friends in Australia…</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

17
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:02,771
<i>They want me to build</i>
<i>a Jade & Jude's there in Sydney.</i>

18
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:07,067
<i>They'll take care of the funding.</i>
<i>I'll be the industrial partner.</i>

19
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:10,320
<i>But I have to stay there.</i>

20
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:13,281
<i>That's good news, right?</i>

21
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:16,993
<i>File your leave, and I'll approve it.</i>

22
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,204
<i>I think I need to just be away.</i>

23
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,041
<i>So, how long?</i>

24
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:26,211
[JORDAN] <i>Might be for good.</i>

25
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,382
What do you think?

26
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:33,259
Mom.

27
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:34,803
Grandpa.

28
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:37,013
Should I push through with this?

29
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,015
I can leave.

30
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,268
I don't have any family left here,

31
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,687
except Billy.

32
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:47,398
She always says

33
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,485
that I'm family.

34
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:53,071
Her best friend.

35
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,160
But that's the problem.

36
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:03,414
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

37
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:06,334
You know,

38
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,254
more than the opportunity,

39
00:02:10,922 --> 00:02:12,799
what really convinced me to go…

40
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:16,219
was my feelings for her.

41
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:20,181
I just thought staying away

42
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,559
might help me move on.

43
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:26,855
Maybe.

44
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:30,483
I hope…

45
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,696
it will help me accept…

46
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,658
that we're really just friends.

47
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:40,952
But what if…

48
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:45,790
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

49
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:47,333
What if I told her…

50
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,503
that I still love her?

51
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:56,175
That I haven't moved on?

52
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:02,724
What if I stay and take a chance?

53
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,475
If Billy asks me to stay,

54
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,896
take a chance on us,

55
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:10,899
then I will stay.

56
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:16,154
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

57
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:18,656
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

58
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:26,748
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:29,269
[BILLY] Oliver, please hurry!
We're already late!

60
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,478
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

61
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:32,188
Oliver!

62
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:33,982
Hurry up, please!

63
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,277
Oh!

64
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:40,905
Oh! What face is that?

65
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:47,370
Billy, I'm really sad.

66
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:49,998
[VOICE CRACKS] Bro Dude is leaving.

67
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,667
He'll only be gone for a short time.

68
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:54,544
He'll be back.

69
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:56,170
But, Billy,

70
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:59,465
what if he meets a new buddy…

71
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,009
[SOBS]

72
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:04,178
…and he doesn't come back?

73
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,180
What if he stays there forever?

74
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:08,975
[BREATH QUIVERS]

75
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:11,853
[SOBS] H-How about you, Billy?

76
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,647
Aren't you sad?

77
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:18,735
Of course I'm sad.

78
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:22,780
But we should be happy for him.

79
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:29,454
Because the opportunities that are
coming his way now?

80
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:32,290
He should've gotten those a long time ago.

81
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:38,379
At least now, he's been given
another chance. Right?

82
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:42,258
- [SNIFFLES]
- [EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:44,218
Mm.

84
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:45,553
[SNIFFLES]

85
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:48,931
[VOICE CRACKS] I will miss him.

86
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,350
[SNIFFLES]

87
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:53,061
What about you, Billy?

88
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:56,105
Will you miss Bro Dude?

89
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:58,775
A lot.

90
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:05,490
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

91
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:08,326
- Oh my! Jordan is already there!
- Come on, give me a smile.

92
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:10,661
- Oliver and I will go get the cake.
- Yes, Auntie.

93
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,455
- I'll only take a minute--
- We'll get the cake.

94
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:13,748
No need. We'll get it.

95
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:16,501
Why did you oversleep?
You never wake up late.

96
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,835
I slept through my alarm.

97
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:20,338
- I'll be quick. Sorry.
- [PRECIOUS] Wait. Didn't you sleep?

98
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:23,132
I saw you were still online
when I woke up.

99
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:25,218
I couldn't sleep.

100
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:28,679
Oliver, go put your shoes on outside.

101
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,389
- Go on, go on.
- I'll be right there, Oliver.

102
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:32,475
[HUMS SOFTLY]

103
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:34,936
- Billy…
- [YELLS] Sorry!

104
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:36,062
Sorry.

105
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,107
Billy, are you okay?

106
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,610
Yes, Auntie. It's just…
I'm just in a hurry.

107
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:44,070
My things are still a mess.

108
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,613
Mm-hmm.

109
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:48,199
Well, you and Jordan
can always video call.

110
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:53,371
We're in different time zones, Auntie.

111
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:54,580
That's difficult.

112
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:56,165
Then go visit him.

113
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:59,293
Plane tickets are expensive.
Never mind.

114
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:00,545
And I'd still need a visa.

115
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,338
Mm-hmm.

116
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:05,383
You can also chat with each other.

117
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:07,385
Send voice messages and stuff.

118
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:09,887
Mm.

119
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:12,140
That's a hassle, Auntie.

120
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:13,975
We're both busy.

121
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:17,186
Mm. Maybe you can spare an hour.

122
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,105
Right?

123
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:20,815
You can make time.

124
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:25,486
One hour will turn into one minute…

125
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,406
and then nothing.

126
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:31,242
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

127
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:32,452
Is it that hard?

128
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:37,165
Of course.

129
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:42,295
We'll have our own separate lives.

130
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:46,382
So you don't want Jordan to leave?

131
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:50,970
I mean, it's okay.

132
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,848
Of course, it's okay.

133
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:56,058
If he wants to leave, he can go ahead.

134
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,187
Billy, how many more excuses
are you going to make

135
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,231
before you admit that
you don't want Jordan to leave?

136
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,610
[EXHALES SOFTLY]
I guess I'm just used to

137
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,070
having him around all the time.

138
00:08:09,572 --> 00:08:12,658
[OLIVER] Auntie, let's go!
They're already livestreaming!

139
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:14,744
They're singing already!

140
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:16,078
Okay!

141
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:19,081
Billy.

142
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,751
It's hard to get used to someone
who isn't yours.

143
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:24,337
[MUSIC BECOMES REFLECTIVE]

144
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:30,343
Maybe it's time to ask yourself,
"Is this really where it ends?"

145
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:37,725
Maybe something in your heart shifted
without you realizing.

146
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,646
Think about it.

147
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:48,277
[REFLECTIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:08:56,911 --> 00:09:02,833
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

149
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:24,897
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:32,363
[GATE RATTLES]

151
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:37,451
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

152
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,415
<i>- Banana split…</i>
<i>- Banana split…</i>

153
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:47,336
[BOTH LAUGHING]

154
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,589
- [YOUNG BILLY] <i>Ah! I win.</i>
- [BOTH LAUGHING]

155
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:50,715
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Hurry up.</i>

156
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:53,843
- [GIGGLING]
<i>- Whatever!</i>

157
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:56,387
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:59,056
- <i>No!</i>
- [LAUGHING]

159
00:09:59,932 --> 00:10:01,475
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>You're ticklish there!</i>

160
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,477
<i>- Stop it!</i>
<i>- Okay, fine.</i>

161
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,812
[SQUEALS, GIGGLES]

162
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:06,731
<i>- Jordan!</i>
- [YOUNG JORDAN LAUGHS]

163
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,608
<i>- I'll really tickle you!</i>
<i>- Hey! Don't!</i>

164
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:10,651
<i>- One more, one more.</i>
<i>- Okay, sure, sure.</i>

165
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:13,571
[YOUNG JORDAN AND YOUNG BILLY]
<i>Banana split!</i>

166
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:20,411
[UPLIFTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,048
- You two are so cute.
- [GIGGLES]

168
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:33,633
- Robbie.
- Boss?

169
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,468
I'll leave Jade & Jude's
in your hands, okay?

170
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:36,510
Mm-hmm!

171
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:38,471
Can you handle it?

172
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:40,264
I remember everything you taught me.

173
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,807
Come on! Of course I can.

174
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:42,850
You didn't bring enough.

175
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,101
[JORDAN, ROBBIE]
Cheers.

176
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:46,896
- [RALPH] Why are you making a toast?
- [ROBBIE] The boss isn't leaving.

177
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,065
He's not leaving.

178
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:50,524
[JORDAN] Thanks for coming, guys.

179
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:51,817
Are you really leaving?

180
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:52,943
If I were you, I'd stay.

181
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,946
- Yeah, right!
- Tell Toni I'll miss her.

182
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,115
Come on!
Wait until she gives birth to leave.

183
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,701
- Then you won't have to miss her.
- You're going to be the godfather.

184
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:03,579
Bro, I can see the plane.
It's totally out of gas.

185
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,248
[CAR ENGINE HUMMING]

186
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:11,796
["IKOT" BY OVER OCTOBER PLAYING]

187
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:34,568
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

188
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:56,507
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

189
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:18,154
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

190
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:41,427
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

191
00:12:56,358 --> 00:13:01,780
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

192
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:23,928
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

193
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:45,991
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

194
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:09,348
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

195
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:30,911
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

196
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:52,933
["IKOT" CONTINUES]

197
00:14:56,645 --> 00:14:57,897
- Cheers!
- [GLASSES CLINKING]

198
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:00,482
For the new name of the bar,
Robbie and Rain!

199
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:01,942
Woohoo!
[LAUGHING]

200
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:04,320
- You all right, Buddy?
- It suits it perfectly, right?

201
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,822
- I thought of it.
- Yeah!

202
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:07,823
Cheers!

203
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,116
- Cheers!
- [GLASSES CLINKING]

204
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:10,534
- Charm, where's Billy?
- Yes?

205
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:11,827
- Huh?
- Where's Billy?

206
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:16,206
I don't know.
Maybe she went to the restroom?

207
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,541
- Okay. Thank you.
- Yes. Go.

208
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:19,209
- You get 0.5 percent.
- That's pretty huge!

209
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:20,836
[CHARM] Guys, cheers!

210
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,837
[MARJ] Cheers, boys!

211
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,714
[ROBBIE] Cheers! Cheers!

212
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:25,966
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- [VALERIE] Oh! Girly!

213
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:30,930
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,098
I don't want Jordan to leave.

215
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:38,395
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:40,356
- [JORDAN] Boo!
- [BILLY] Whoa!

217
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,523
What the…

218
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,150
- [GRUNTS]
- Stop moping on your own!

219
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:45,319
It's not allowed, all right?

220
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:46,904
I got you a beer.

221
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:51,075
[LAUGHING SOFTLY]

222
00:15:51,158 --> 00:15:52,201
What?

223
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,287
What's so funny?

224
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:56,330
Huh?

225
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:00,459
After you got my mind all messed up…

226
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,838
you tell me you're leaving

227
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:07,257
and you don't know when you'll be back?

228
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:08,926
What's with that?

229
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,137
All right, I'll stay then.

230
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:17,267
If you want, I can stay.

231
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:21,647
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

232
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:22,898
Because, Billy…

233
00:16:25,567 --> 00:16:26,902
they're still there.

234
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:29,863
What is?

235
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:31,949
My feelings for you.

236
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:38,872
[WARM MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:46,338
I know it's a good opportunity
for me to be in Australia.

238
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:50,300
And I know it's the right thing
for me to leave.

239
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:53,887
But I can't be at peace
because I know I'll be leaving you behind.

240
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:56,932
I'll be miles away from you.

241
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:00,978
[SIGHS]

242
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:03,939
Dude, I've tried just being friends.

243
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:08,485
I really tried to go back to
how I was before, but…

244
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:10,612
it's no use.

245
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,782
I love you too much.

246
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:21,415
[WARM MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:26,837
I wish we could be more than friends,
but I know it's not what you want.

248
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,381
That's why…

249
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,303
when I got the chance to go to Australia…

250
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:37,931
I thought…

251
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:40,934
maybe it's fate.

252
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:45,898
Maybe it's fate telling me
that I need to go away.

253
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:50,569
Because…

254
00:17:53,655 --> 00:18:00,537
[WARM MUSIC CONTINUES]

255
00:18:01,371 --> 00:18:04,041
Because I don't think I can be friends

256
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:06,710
when it hurts this much.

257
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,844
Maybe distance could help.

258
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,431
Who knows? Maybe…

259
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:23,310
one day I could learn
to just be friends again.

260
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,778
If you tell me

261
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,364
that you love me back…

262
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,536
and that there's a chance
for us to be together,

263
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:43,080
and I mean

264
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:45,749
really together…

265
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,796
I won't leave.

266
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,008
Dude.

267
00:19:00,055 --> 00:19:04,017
I would give all my time
and focus to you.

268
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:05,185
To LoveList too.

269
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,855
I would help you take care of Oliver.

270
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:10,524
Even your father.

271
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:14,653
Your dreams will become my dreams.

272
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:17,072
And I…

273
00:19:17,781 --> 00:19:19,324
I will make sure

274
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:23,287
that I'll always be by your side
when you need me.

275
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:26,331
Just say the word.

276
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,917
I'll stay.

277
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:36,758
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:52,024
Whenever I'm happy or sad,

279
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,359
even when I'm mad…

280
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:02,034
you're the first person I want to see.

281
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:06,580
You are always there for me.

282
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:12,961
But do you know what
the best gift I can give you is?

283
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:22,054
It's to learn to live without you.

284
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:33,815
You need to go to Australia.

285
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:42,157
You have done so much for me.

286
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:46,954
And I will forever be grateful.

287
00:20:56,463 --> 00:20:58,173
But it's your turn.

288
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:05,097
Choose yourself this time.

289
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:10,227
What about you?

290
00:21:14,898 --> 00:21:16,275
I'll be okay.

291
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:23,907
[MUSIC TURNS EMOTIONAL]

292
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:40,215
One last dance?

293
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:45,095
Of course.

294
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:51,393
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:13,623
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:36,897
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:22:51,912 --> 00:22:58,919
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

298
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:03,381
[MUSIC FADES]

299
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:09,262
Boss.

300
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,850
- [ROBBIE] Don't leave.
- Yes.

301
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,685
[EXCLAIMS, LAUGHS]

302
00:23:15,769 --> 00:23:16,937
- Take care.
- Yup.

303
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,688
We'll hold the fort down here.
Don't worry.

304
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:20,816
Auntie Pres.

305
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:26,905
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

306
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:29,116
Hey.

307
00:23:33,203 --> 00:23:35,622
I'm gonna miss you so much.

308
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:38,208
I'll miss you too.

309
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:44,256
Dude.

310
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:55,350
Don't see me off anymore.

311
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:57,978
I might change my mind.

312
00:24:01,189 --> 00:24:02,399
Go on.

313
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,528
[BILLY] Get going.

314
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:09,990
- Take care, brother.
- Bye. Safe flight.

315
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,492
Have a safe flight.

316
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:30,010
[BILLY] <i>I've always been hurt,</i>
<i>angry, and scared all my life.</i>

317
00:24:30,093 --> 00:24:31,845
<i>Love has always been there.</i>

318
00:24:31,928 --> 00:24:34,264
<i>But I know I took a step back.</i>

319
00:24:34,931 --> 00:24:38,435
<i>Now that everything is better, I'm ready.</i>

320
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:41,104
<i>But I do wonder…</i>

321
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:42,898
<i>Is it too late?</i>

322
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:46,902
<i>Do I still know how to love?</i>

323
00:24:47,944 --> 00:24:49,571
<i>Am I still capable of loving?</i>

324
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:54,117
<i>But when I think of</i>
<i>the people I care about,</i>

325
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:56,119
<i>I realize that</i>

326
00:24:57,287 --> 00:24:59,873
<i>I never forgot how to love.</i>

327
00:25:03,084 --> 00:25:05,962
<i>Maybe that's enough to make me hopeful.</i>

328
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:08,173
<i>Someday,</i>

329
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:11,301
<i>I'll find my way back to love.</i>

330
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:18,225
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:28,902
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:25:37,911 --> 00:25:39,412
- [SILLY SFX]
- [LAUGHS]

333
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:42,332
Sorry, Director. We were about
to say a line. Is it okay…

334
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:53,510
Yes, of course. I will help.

335
00:25:58,556 --> 00:26:00,100
- Vroom!
- [SILLY SFX]

336
00:26:00,183 --> 00:26:01,685
[LAUGH SFX]

337
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:03,436
[DIRECTOR] Cut!

338
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,397
Never mind it.

339
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,732
Ralph and Yani said they'd fix it.

340
00:26:07,816 --> 00:26:09,484
Did Val do that?

341
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:12,237
Hey.

342
00:26:13,613 --> 00:26:14,948
- What's that?
- ["OH NO" SFX]

343
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:16,533
Imaginary phone. [LAUGHS]

344
00:26:25,625 --> 00:26:29,087
Yes, chief. A hundred percent sure.

345
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:31,006
I tasted it myself.

346
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:33,300
So if there are le--leftovers,

347
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:34,467
I'm safe too.

348
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:36,052
Sorry, Director.

349
00:26:36,136 --> 00:26:37,178
[LAUGHING]

350
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:38,513
I ad-libbed so many times.

351
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:45,270
[JOLLY MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:26:45,353 --> 00:26:46,813
Wait, mister. I'm coming too. [LAUGHS]

353
00:26:46,896 --> 00:26:48,273
- [LAUGHS]
- [DIRECTOR] Cut!

354
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:01,911
Sorry.

355
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:03,830
You got dragged.

356
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:06,207
[BOTH LAUGH]

357
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,625
[MAJA] He just laughed at himself.

358
00:27:09,919 --> 00:27:12,172
[SILLY SFX]

359
00:27:13,923 --> 00:27:15,175
[STAFF] What is it?

360
00:27:15,258 --> 00:27:16,676
[LAUGHING] It's…

361
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,261
- Supposed to go that way?
- Yeah.

362
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:22,265
[STAFF] You're holding the phone
upside down, Ms. Dimps.

363
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:23,850
- ["OH NO" SFX]
- [GIGGLES] Sorry.

364
00:27:23,933 --> 00:27:26,311
The screen's all black to me.
I'm sorry, Director.

365
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:40,492
My God.

366
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:42,243
[ALL CHUCKLING]

367
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:44,329
It's filled to the brim.

368
00:27:44,412 --> 00:27:47,207
- How thirsty are you?
- Are you just gonna sip it from the table?

369
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:48,708
It's all for you.

370
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:52,045
[STAFF] "For us."

371
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:54,839
- It's for us. For us two.
- [ERROR BUZZ SFX]

372
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:56,925
- [LAUGHS] Sorry.
- [LAUGH SFX]

373
00:27:57,675 --> 00:28:00,553
…when we were almost separated by the

374
00:28:01,846 --> 00:28:03,306
Commission Welfare?

375
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:05,934
- [ERROR BUZZ SFX]
- [LAUGHING] What was it?

376
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,478
Social Welfare Commission. Okay.

377
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:34,587
[MUSIC FADES]

378
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:41,136
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

379
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:18,923
[MUSIC ENDS]
